<title>GERMANY: MG expects favourable developments 1996/97.</title>
<headline>MG expects favourable developments 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering group Metallgesellschaft AG said on Friday that it expects continued favourable development in the current business year.</p>
<p>Metallgesellschaft said earnings growth would form a foundation for the group to again start paying out dividends.</p>
<p>The group said in a statement containing its results for 1995/96: &quot;For the current year, the group expects favourable developments to continue and to increase our earnings power, which will form a foundation for a renewed dividend payout.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +59 69 756525</p>
</text>
